claudinite-isolation notices only THAT a file names a mount path, not whether
it exists, and CLAUDE.md carries an `accept` for it, so on the one file that
must name a mount path that barrier is switched off entirely. The consequence
is concrete: the stale reference is the Setup-script paste target, the only
thing that puts Flutter in a cloud session.

